9
00:00:20,165 --> 00:00:22,761
A patient develops an unusual infection

10
00:00:22,761 --> 00:00:24,259
after an endoscopy.

11
00:00:24,923 --> 00:00:26,060
Was it the scope?

12
00:00:26,690 --> 00:00:28,236
Who else was exposed?

13
00:00:28,877 --> 00:00:30,916
Only your records can answer that.

14
00:00:33,831 --> 00:00:36,079
Traceability links four things for every

15
00:00:36,079 --> 00:00:39,690
procedure. The scope, say scope seven,

16
00:00:39,731 --> 00:00:42,178
used on patient forty-four seventy-one.

17
00:00:42,844 --> 00:00:45,356
The reprocessing cycle, cycle eleven

18
00:00:45,356 --> 00:00:47,070
forty-two, which passed.

19
00:00:47,747 --> 00:00:50,111
And the operator, technician twelve.

20
00:00:50,848 --> 00:00:53,360
With that chain, a suspected transmission

21
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:56,048
can be traced to exactly who was exposed.

22
00:00:59,198 --> 00:01:00,869
Around that chain sit four more

23
00:01:00,869 --> 00:01:04,196
safeguards. Microbiological surveillance

24
00:01:04,196 --> 00:01:06,492
of scopes at defined intervals, with

25
00:01:06,492 --> 00:01:09,060
defined actions on a positive result.

26
00:01:09,749 --> 00:01:12,393
Reprocessor validation, including final

27
00:01:12,393 --> 00:01:13,891
rinse water quality.

28
00:01:14,593 --> 00:01:16,524
Records of every cycle.

29
00:01:17,213 --> 00:01:19,737
And a damage and repair log, since a scope

30
00:01:19,737 --> 00:01:22,033
back from repair is reprocessed before

31
00:01:22,033 --> 00:01:22,641
use.

32
00:01:25,798 --> 00:01:28,094
If transmission is suspected, first

33
00:01:28,094 --> 00:01:29,387
quarantine the scope.

34
00:01:30,087 --> 00:01:31,525
Don't reprocess it:

35
00:01:31,577 --> 00:01:33,304
that destroys the evidence.

36
00:01:34,005 --> 00:01:37,090
Notify infection control and microbiology.

37
00:01:37,779 --> 00:01:40,051
Retrieve the records of every exposed

38
00:01:40,051 --> 00:01:43,488
patient. Review practice, and sample the

39
00:01:43,488 --> 00:01:45,155
scope and reprocessor.

40
00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:47,474
Check its repair history.

41
00:01:48,104 --> 00:01:51,025
Then consider patient notification, report

42
00:01:51,025 --> 00:01:53,380
externally where required, and write it

43
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:53,809
up.

44
00:01:56,965 --> 00:01:59,316
Most of these failures share one cause:

45
00:01:59,345 --> 00:02:02,444
time pressure. When a list runs late and

46
00:02:02,444 --> 00:02:04,716
one scope is available, a technician

47
00:02:04,716 --> 00:02:06,506
decides alone whether brushing was

48
00:02:06,506 --> 00:02:09,716
adequate. That decision shouldn't rest on

49
00:02:09,716 --> 00:02:11,009
individual courage.

50
00:02:11,699 --> 00:02:14,343
It needs written policy, a defined right

51
00:02:14,343 --> 00:02:16,951
to hold a scope back, adequate inventory

52
00:02:16,951 --> 00:02:19,555
and staffing, and recorded deviations.

53
00:02:22,665 --> 00:02:23,995
Final knowledge check.

54
00:02:24,694 --> 00:02:27,026
A list is running late, one scope is

55
00:02:27,026 --> 00:02:29,502
available, and a technician is unsure the

56
00:02:29,502 --> 00:02:31,060
brushing was adequate.

57
00:02:31,750 --> 00:02:33,524
What should decide the outcome?

58
00:02:34,178 --> 00:02:35,904
Pause here and think it through.

59
00:02:43,198 --> 00:02:45,662
Written policy and a defined right to hold

60
00:02:45,662 --> 00:02:47,765
the scope back, supported by named

61
00:02:47,765 --> 00:02:49,917
management, not the courage of one

62
00:02:49,917 --> 00:02:51,499
technician under pressure.

63
00:02:52,126 --> 00:02:54,446
The root causes are inadequate inventory

64
00:02:54,446 --> 00:02:57,102
and capacity, so escalate with the patient

65
00:02:57,102 --> 00:02:59,718
risk stated, and record the deviation.

66
00:03:02,798 --> 00:03:06,193
Let's recap! Trace every procedure:

67
00:03:06,198 --> 00:03:09,186
scope, patient, cycle and operator.

68
00:03:09,888 --> 00:03:12,484
If transmission is suspected, quarantine

69
00:03:12,484 --> 00:03:14,475
the scope and never reprocess it.

70
00:03:15,188 --> 00:03:16,967
And protect staff from pressure with

71
00:03:16,967 --> 00:03:19,919
policy, inventory and management backing.

72
00:03:20,573 --> 00:03:22,964
That completes this module on flexible

73
00:03:22,964 --> 00:03:24,691
